  "priorExpiration": "2017-02-14",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Saf-C 5702.04 Notification of Disposition.\n\n(a) The clerks of circuit and superior courts shall report the plea, court disposition, and the sentence imposed, if any, or any subsequent modification of the original sentence, of any person brought before the court on a felony, misdemeanor, or violation charge pursuant to RSA 106-B:14, I to the central repository as soon as possible, but not later than 90 days after the case has been disposed of.\n\n(b) The report shall:\n\n(1) Be on a certified abstract of finding, or a reasonable facsimile thereof, and\n\n(2) Contain at a minimum, the:\n\na. Name, address, and date of birth of each defendant;\n\nb. Date of offense;\n\nc. Name of offense;\n\nd. Track number;\n\ne. Statutory citation for which the defendant was originally charged;\n\nf. Any subsequent modification thereof;\n\ng. The court, date of sentence, the plea, court disposition, and sentence, if any; or\n\nh. Any subsequent modification of the original sentence.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note at Chapter Heading for Saf-C 5700) #6704, eff 3-3-98, EXPIRED: 3-3-06\n\nNew. #8591, INTERIM, eff 3-24-06, EXPIRES: 9-20-06; ss by #8651, eff 6-2-06, EXPIRED: 6-2-14\n\nNew. #11157, INTERIM, eff 8-18-16, EXPIRED: 2-14-17\n\nNew. #12132, eff 3-17-17",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/saf-c5700.html"
